WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:04.713
- Narrator: Imagine giving
birth to a 24 pound baby.

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.600
That's three times the size

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.443
of an average human newborn. Ouch.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.270
But for kiwi birds,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.480
giant chicks are the norm.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.370
Females lay a single egg up
to 20% of their body weight,

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.100
yet when you check out

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.760
other extreme births
in the animal kingdom,

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:27.253
the kiwi can consider itself lucky.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.080
Shingleback lizards also
have a tough pregnancy.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:39.270
These reptiles usually have
one to two babies at a time,

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.810
which doesn't sound so bad,

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.060
until you realize that combined,

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.320
the babies make up a third
of the mother's body weight.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.260
That's like a human giving
birth to a seven year old!

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.060
But a baby doesn't need
to be big to be difficult.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.240
Take the porcupine.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.000
Those sharp spines
protect it from predators,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.163
but they're sometimes not so fun for Mom.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.570
You see, baby porcupines,
called porcupettes,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.640
aren't hairless like most rodent newborns.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.733
These guys are born fully quilled.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.200
Normally, this isn't a problem for Mom,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.320
since the quills are soft at birth,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.250
and gradually harden
over the next few hours.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.210
But complications can arise

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.460
when the porcupettes are
facing the wrong direction,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.490
because their quills can get caught

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:36.020
in the birth canal on the way out.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.150
Speaking of birth canals,

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.293
the spotted hyena has an interesting one.

00:01:42.291 --> 00:01:45.680
Females have phallic-like genitalia.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.690
The scientific term for
this is pseudo-penis,

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.340
and they give birth out
of the pseudo-penis,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.310
which will sometimes rip
apart in the process.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:02:00.150
It's not only painful, it can be lethal.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:05.150
In fact, about 15% of first-time
mothers die giving birth.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:08.830
But, believe it or not,

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.723
a species of velvet
spider has it even worse.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.650
You know how some animals
chew up food for their babies?

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:22.650
Well, Stegodyphus lineatus
takes this to a whole new level.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.520
Right after she lays an egg sac,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.300
the mother's tissues start to degrade.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.310
Once the spiderlings hatch,

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.670
she regurgitates her
own liquified insides,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.883
and the babies chow down.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.070
Nine days later, they suck
up the last of her fluids,

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.980
and strike out on their own,

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.840
leaving nothing but an empty husk.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.650
Thanks Mom.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.640
But childbirth isn't just dangerous

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.010
or uncomfortable for mothers.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:55.970
With some animals, the
baby has it pretty rough.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:58.460
Take the Tasmanian devil.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.530
The mom gives birth to
up to 50 joeys at a time,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.850
each the size of a raisin.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.680
They have to crawl from
the mother's birth canal,

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.460
over her body, and into her pouch,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.900
where they'll snuggle up
for another four months.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.980
But there's a catch.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:19.810
Mom has only four nipples in her pouch.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.350
So right from birth

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.550
the joeys are literally on
a mad dash for their lives,

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.240
and only the strongest four will make it.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.313
Talk about sibling rivalry, huh?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.790
Overall, one thing is clear:

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.250
humans aren't the only
ones who have it rough

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.923
when it comes to giving birth.

00:03:39.463 --> 00:03:42.340
What's the craziest animal fact you know?

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.580
Tell us in the comments
and thanks for watching.

